  <constraints>
    <constraint source="Owner decision Q1 (BINDING)">
      New enum member names are EXACTLY `Model1` and `Model2` (drop `-Shared`/`-Dedicated` qualifiers entirely).
      New Dataverse option-set labels are EXACTLY `"Model1"` and `"Model2"`. Integer values stay `0` for Model1
      and `1` for Model2 (preserves the `Extend-DataverseEnvironmentSchema-v3.3.ps1:211,217-218` integer alignment).
    </constraint>

    <constraint source="Owner decision Q2 + Q3 (BINDING)">
      NO H12c migration handler. NO compat shim. NO dual-path renderer. Greenfield state (zero completed H12c
      phases in production Cosmos) accepts natural invalidation. Task 223's `TenancyModelParserTests.EnumToString_*`
      tripwire tests are REWRITTEN to pin the NEW `Model1`/`Model2` strings, not the historical
      `Model1Shared`/`Model2Dedicated` strings. The BINDING preservation invariant from T223 is EXPLICITLY spent.
    </constraint>

    <constraint source="Item 3 vs Item 4 scope split (owner-decided, BINDING)">
      Task 224 is MECHANICAL RENAME only. Handler branch BODIES are unchanged — do NOT redirect the semantic that
      Model1 previously routed to (shared-platform code path). Task 225 (Item 4) will redirect BOTH `Model1` and
      `Model2` branches to the dedicated code path AND retire the shared-platform code + `model1-*.bicep` seven-
      surface atomic. Any attempt in T224 to also redirect Model1's routing is scope creep — file it into T225 or
      escalate per root CLAUDE.md §6.
    </constraint>

    <constraint source="INCOMING §5 Item 3 (BINDING)">
      "Do NOT relabel" — the concern was silent misclassification of existing dedicated customers if value 1's
      string label just flipped in place. Given the greenfield state (owner confirmed no customers), the risk is
      moot. But the SEMANTIC still holds for the future: Model1 = Spaarke-hosted dedicated stamp; Model2 = Customer-
      hosted dedicated stamp. This informs T224's inline comment updates + the Dataverse column description.
    </constraint>

    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §6.5 (ADR Conflict Resolution Protocol)">
      Path C (pivot to comply with D-12). No Path A/B expected. Silent violation FORBIDDEN.
    </constraint>

    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §8 test-modifying override">
      Task modifies `*Tests/**` — UNCONDITIONAL FULL rigor + UNCONDITIONAL Step 9.5 quality gates
      (code-review + adr-check).
    </constraint>

    <constraint source="ADR-038 §7 KEEP-path forcing-function discipline">
      Test modifications (~37 fixture sites) are mechanical rename OR rewrite of T223's H12c-tripwire tests. Do NOT
      scope-narrow, `[Skip]`, or delete any test whose premise remains valid post-rename. ArchTest suite MUST remain
      326/326 (verified 5× this project already; the enum rename is intra-namespace and should not affect
      ArchTest outcomes).
    </constraint>

    <constraint source="ADR-028 A4 (posture preservation)">
      T224 introduces NO new `.WithClientSecret(...)` sites, NO new `ClientSecretCredential(...)` constructions.
      Zero credential surface changes.
    </constraint>

    <constraint source="ADR-044 (canonical GUID/string patterns)">
      Not affected — this task renames an option-set label + enum member, neither of which are GUID surface.
    </constraint>
  </constraints>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>
      If preflight grep finds ANY Cosmos row with `CompletedPhases[].Phase == "H12c"` in a live environment
      (production or staging) — STOP. Owner decision Q2 rested on greenfield state; a completed H12c phase invalidates
      that premise and reopens the H12c migration question.
    </trigger>
    <trigger>
      If `dotnet test tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/` drops below 326/326 post-change — STOP. The enum rename should not
      regress any ArchTest (all tests operate on type-level structure that is unchanged; string content in tests is
      mechanical rename).
    </trigger>
    <trigger>
      If `dotnet test src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/` shows more than 23 baseline failures
      (task 221 domain: 17× FileKvSecretManifestTests + 6× CustomerRunGuardModulePostConfigureTests) — STOP + stash-
      and-compare to isolate whether the new failure is T224-caused or a downstream shift.
    </trigger>
    <trigger>
      If the mechanical rename introduces a compile error not in the enumerated in-scope files — STOP and audit for
      scope creep. Likely candidate: a parallel worktree added a new consumer of `TenancyModel.Model1Shared` or
      `Model2Dedicated` since Task 223's master merge.
    </trigger>
    <trigger>
      If a hit surfaces in ANY of these HOT locations, STOP: (a) `.github/workflows/**`; (b) `infrastructure/bicep/**`
      (Item 4 territory — do NOT touch); (c) `.claude/skills/provision-environment/**` (L3 operator skill);
      (d) any file under `projects/unified-access-control-r2/**` or `projects/auth-v*/**` (parallel-worktree hot-path).
    </trigger>
    <trigger>
      If the executor is tempted to ALSO retire `HandleModel1BranchAsync` (H2b), `SharedPlatformOpenAiEndpoint`, or
      any shared-platform code path — STOP. That is Item 4 (Task 225) scope per owner-decided split. Escalate per
      root §6 if uncertain.
    </trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>T223's `TenancyModel` enum + `TenancyModelParser` at `Core/Models/TenancyModel.cs` — this is a name-only rename of existing surface, not new-component introduction.</existing>
    <extension>N/A — this task extends the T223 enum by renaming its two members. It is a rename, not new surface.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The pre-D-12 string labels (`Model1Shared`, `Model2Dedicated`) misrepresent the D-12 semantic: post-D-12 both models are dedicated stamps (no more "shared" tier); the `-Shared` qualifier on Model1 is actively misleading, and `-Dedicated` on Model2 is redundant. Leaving the strings unchanged means every future contributor + operator + maker sees mislabeled option-set values, invites new silent-misclassification bugs at API boundaries, and defers Item 4's inevitable renames. This closes atomically at T224.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

